                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "13617fce-0849-3552-9c4f-41a9e77daaed",
                        "entry_id": "524b7049-e676-399e-b783-c91af6606a37",
                        "glosses": [
                            "по суеверным представлениям — послужить признаком, заранее возвещающим о том, что будет"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f0ec64af-ff6e-4318-a92b-d0c8abc9cc37",
                        "source_entry_id": "524b7049-e676-399e-b783-c91af6606a37",
                        "source_sense_id": "13617fce-0849-3552-9c4f-41a9e77daaed",
                        "target_lang_word": "foreshadow",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "foreshadow",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c00aa9e2-1129-3694-a79f-974e013a4b11",
                                        "entry_id": "ecabc771-434d-3a20-8f70-ab1a56939574",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To presage, or suggest something in advance."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "06ad63f7-0372-4c6a-ab88-e87ac6cd4b7a",
                                                "sense_id": "c00aa9e2-1129-3694-a79f-974e013a4b11",
                                                "text": "It all sounds to us remarkably nineteenth-century; Petrarch's romantic sentiments foreshadow with uncanny precision those of Dante Gabriel Rossetti or Alfred de Musset."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "177c7d8a-fa80-4b41-9b4e-411bb405e76e",
                                                "sense_id": "c00aa9e2-1129-3694-a79f-974e013a4b11",
                                                "text": "If there is a significant or surprising event in the story, it must be foreshadowed earlier on. When the event that was foreshadowed occurs, that's the payoff."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "6e4408da-5127-4efd-8a6a-6f1618c6254f",
                        "source_entry_id": "524b7049-e676-399e-b783-c91af6606a37",
                        "source_sense_id": "13617fce-0849-3552-9c4f-41a9e77daaed",
                        "target_lang_word": "portend",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "portend",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a007b7b5-37e3-34a1-976d-f43d5e186a29",
                                        "entry_id": "4776f1bc-ef91-3e03-a6c1-131124e8fe37",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To serve as a warning or omen of."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ffd03902-7886-44a3-be66-1157176ff790",
                                                "sense_id": "a007b7b5-37e3-34a1-976d-f43d5e186a29",
                                                "text": "A kingdom they portend thee, but what kingdom, / Real or allegoric, I discern not; Nor when: eternal sure--as without end,"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bb6f6351-d743-36b5-afd1-ff2d77354f23",
                                        "entry_id": "4776f1bc-ef91-3e03-a6c1-131124e8fe37",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To signify; to denote."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "37d47f73-b4cd-446d-9a12-3985f12ac7ff",
                                                "sense_id": "bb6f6351-d743-36b5-afd1-ff2d77354f23",
                                                "text": "Let it be known that the Rapture portends the End of Days."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2aa0031a-5151-43b5-877e-6834191820e1",
                                                "sense_id": "bb6f6351-d743-36b5-afd1-ff2d77354f23",
                                                "text": "How alive these poems are with the visual specifics of what he so closely observes, how full of elegance, terror and hope. They portend a poet of major craft, of deep feeling, and of fine intelligence."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8027a259-1d61-452d-823b-687204f4d335",
                                                "sense_id": "bb6f6351-d743-36b5-afd1-ff2d77354f23",
                                                "text": "When the staccato, Neptunes-ian single “Boyfriend” was released in March, musical prognosticators were quick to peg the album it portended, Believe, as Justin Bieber’s Justified, a grown-and-sexy, R&B-centric departure that evolved millennial teenybopper Justin Timberlake into one of the unifying pop-music figures of the aughts."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a4cb8825-ff8b-404a-8419-24a704674383",
                        "source_entry_id": "524b7049-e676-399e-b783-c91af6606a37",
                        "source_sense_id": "13617fce-0849-3552-9c4f-41a9e77daaed",
                        "target_lang_word": "presage",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "presage",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "037b74ad-f5ea-31a2-bc34-331f136666c5",
                                        "entry_id": "2e361edf-0273-3c4d-bacf-0651dc27d764",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A warning of a future event; an omen."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "229e3ae7-6d0d-4309-93bf-77f333cb0ebd",
                                                "sense_id": "037b74ad-f5ea-31a2-bc34-331f136666c5",
                                                "text": "Speak frankly, Mirzes—nor believe thy words, / Whatever black preſages they contain, / Subjoin'd to all Trophonius hath foretold, / Can change my firm reſolves, or blunt my ſword."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5c3a337f-79ac-3c33-bc43-680ce2ac72e3",
                                        "entry_id": "2e361edf-0273-3c4d-bacf-0651dc27d764",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An intuition of a future event; a presentiment."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8e84b528-e74d-43da-9783-c7ae92db5552",
                                                "sense_id": "5c3a337f-79ac-3c33-bc43-680ce2ac72e3",
                                                "text": "Glad was I when I reached the other bank. / Now for a better country. Vain presage!"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "presage",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "79e18584-ddcc-3593-8a5e-0274bc83e0da",
                                        "entry_id": "0791061e-b933-3e4c-a0c9-94dccbb81ed0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To predict or foretell something."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d7fc140a-7a8f-4cc6-98be-d13b05caa734",
                                                "sense_id": "79e18584-ddcc-3593-8a5e-0274bc83e0da",
                                                "text": "If I may truſt the flattering truth of ſleepe, / My dreames preſage ſome ioyfull newes at hand : / My boſomes L. ſits lightly in his throne : / And all this day an vnaccuſtom’d ſpirit, / Lifts me aboue the ground with cheatfull thoughts […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e5833c8c-17c4-4cb3-ba72-e21a296e61b7",
                                                "sense_id": "79e18584-ddcc-3593-8a5e-0274bc83e0da",
                                                "text": "That brief moment after the election four years ago, when many Americans thought Mr. Obama’s election would presage a new, less fractious political era, now seems very much a thing of the past."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c0ada764-e142-30ca-be3f-da6d67a9ac31",
                                        "entry_id": "0791061e-b933-3e4c-a0c9-94dccbb81ed0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To make a prediction."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "891a3c08-6349-3422-80ad-5cdbf75a528b",
                                        "entry_id": "0791061e-b933-3e4c-a0c9-94dccbb81ed0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To have a presentiment of; to feel beforehand; to foreknow."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
